==French==

===Etymology===
Feminine past participle of {{m|fr|sortir}}; from {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|sortīrī}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|sortior||cast lots, divide, receive}}, possibly influenced by a derivative of {{m|la|surgō||get up, arise}}. Compare {{cog|it|sortire||produce}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-sortie.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|f}}

# {{l|en|exit}}, {{l|en|way out}}
#: {{ant|fr|entrée}}
# act of [[exit]]ing
# {{l|en|end}}; final part of
# {{l|en|release}} {{gloss|of a film, book, album etc}}
#: {{syn|fr|édition|parution}}
# (school) {{l|en|outing}}, {{l|en|trip}} {{gloss|lasting no longer than a day}}
# {{lb|fr|military}} {{l|en|leave}}, {{l|en|sally}}, {{l|en|sortie}}
# {{lb|fr|electronics}} {{l|en|output}}, {{l|en|connector}}
#: {{syn|fr|prise}}

====Usage notes====
The meaning "end, release" is used of things such as school, theater etc. where a literal "exit" also occurs.

